        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add secure read-only MCP server",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a disabled-by-default Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint at `/mcp`\n- expose only cached tweet search and cached thread reads\n- keep DMs, live X access, OpenAI calls, filesystem access, and all mutations outside the MCP boundary\n- add independent bearer authentication, exact Host/Origin validation, loopback-origin enforcement, request/rate/concurrency limits, and read-only SQLite access\n- document local, Codex, and Cloudflare Access deployment\n\n## Why\n\nBirdclaw already holds the useful research data locally, but agents currently need direct machine access or bespoke commands to query it. This adds a small, auditable MCP surface that can be hosted by the existing Birdclaw process without reusing the write-capable web session or changing the existing personal setup.\n\n## Validation\n\n- official MCP SDK `Client` + `StreamableHTTPClientTransport` end-to-end smoke\n- focused security and database no-write regression coverage\n- formatting and lint checks on touched files\n- strict standalone TypeScript compile of the MCP surface\n- frozen offline lockfile validation\n- docs site build\n",
